<chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude"  xml:id="chapter-13-intro">
  <title>Week 13</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      At the end of this week you should be able to...
    </p>
    <objectives>
      <ul>
        <li></li>
        <li>understand the purpose of writing methods without a return type</li>
        <li>Trace the flow of control during the execution of a program using multiple classes</li>
        <li>Identify type errors resulting from use of multiple classes and instance method calls</li>
        <li>Illustrate the full scope of variables and visibility within classes in Java</li>
        <li>Use a debugger to examine the heap</li>
        <li>Trace the flow of control during the execution of a program using side effects</li>
        <li>Read a program using side effects and/or nested loops and explain what it does</li>
      </ul>
    </objectives>
  </introduction>
  <xi:include href="sec-references.ptx"/>
  <xi:include href="sec-passby.ptx"/>
  <xi:include href="sec-two-dimensional-arrays.ptx"/>
</chapter>
